EF AI Workspace: the web client behaves like a phone app (#238). Owner decision 2026-10-26, after an audit of the
installed app on an iPhone 13 Pro Max (items 1-6 of the audit; brand.css holds the touch-screen styles).

- index.html: `viewport-fit=cover`, so iPhone applies the safe-area spacing the drawer, the sheets, the top bar and the
  composer already ask for (env(safe-area-inset-*) is 0 without it).
- utils/efaiwApp.ts: keeps the browser's install offer (`beforeinstallprompt`, Android and desktop Chromium), which can
  arrive before the app mounts (main.jsx imports it first); `useEfInstall` for the menu row; iPhone and installed-app
  detection.
- Account menu (Nav/AccountSettings.tsx): «تثبيت التطبيق» when the browser offers installation (its dialog) or on
  iPhone (the hint); never inside the installed app.
- components/EfApp/EfAppShell.tsx, mounted in routes/Root.tsx:
  - the iPhone hint: once, outside the installed app, «اضغط زر المشاركة ثم إضافة إلى الشاشة الرئيسية». Its state lives
    in utils/efaiwApp.ts so the skills tip (Chat/Input/EfSkillsTip.tsx) waits while it is open: one card at a time;
  - the new-version bar: a new service worker took over an open page (upstream's sw-heal reloads only pages that
    stop answering), so «نسخة جديدة من بصير متاحة — تحديث»; back in the foreground the worker is re-checked at most
    every ten minutes.
- Sign-in and sign-up (Auth/LoginForm.tsx, Auth/Registration.tsx): the e-mail keyboard, no capital first letter, no
  autocorrect.
- Strings: six `com_efaiw_*` keys (English here, Arabic in ar.json).
- Tests: utils/__tests__/efaiwApp.test.ts, components/EfApp/__tests__/EfAppShell.spec.tsx.

